{"parentUuid":"a15c0064-a9ae-4675-b3a7-e0c50bc5fd90","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChQ8kvjDTDwCv4UXMSCja","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KSrgzyD8WKaBMNdLqZtsst","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"/Users/kenneth/Library/Application Support/Claude/side-session-notes/local_cd3120f7-030a-4af8-a6d1-28ecae789f1a/\" && sed -n 332,441p misrouted-failures-simple-or-not.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":696,"cache_read_input_tokens":127924,"output_tokens":465,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":330},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":696,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":465,"cache_read_input_tokens":127924,"cache_creation_input_tokens":696,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":696},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":1340,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01KSrgzyD8WKaBMNdLqZtsst":{"command":"cd \"/Users/kenneth/Library/Application Support/Claude/side-session-notes/local_cd3120f7-030a-4af8-a6d1-28ecae789f1a/\" && sed -n 332,441p misrouted-failures-simple-or-not.md"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"d038a58a-3c07-424f-9a83-5263b2f61ad7","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011ChQ8kvXJzgSwwo4Qbre8C","requestRef":"b52cc373-2183-457e-a378-358d6012761e","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"47f88936-e8f3-4ff7-9f9e-6565f3ae02bf","timestamp":"2026-11-25T18:39:50.423Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","madeBy":"model","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Library/Application Support/Claude/side-session-notes/local_cd3120f7-030a-4af8-a6d1-28ecae789f1a","sessionId":"b575a9e5-080c-46d7-b71a-f5842e099a04","version":"2.1.330","gitBranch":"claude/misrouted-failures","slug":"linear-finding-kay-of-b575a9e5-080c-46d7-b71a-f5842e099a04","dataFlowOn":true}
{"parentUuid":"47f88936-e8f3-4ff7-9f9e-6565f3ae02bf","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"72013b54-b18f-48cf-ab14-3227cd513d22","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KSrgzyD8WKaBMNdLqZtsst","type":"tool_result","content":"## The server\n\n**The app sends something the server refuses** (a field a newer app added, a model removed from the\naliases, an empty alias setting).\n- Where: `v2/errors.py:68-76` (`REFUSALS`), `v2/gateway.py:206-211`, `v2/upstream.py`, and\n  `v2/views.py:172-175, 267-270`. Answered \"The request is not valid.\" or \"This model is not\n  available.\", with one log line of the code only.\n- Whose: ours, since our code is on both ends. Kenneth on 2026-11-15: \"Treat them as unexpected\n  errors.\" Never made to happen.\n- Change: raise in place of each refusal, so the top handler reports it. The app already treats the\n  server's error answer as ours.\n- **Simple.**\n\n**A paid Chargebee event that matches nothing.**\n- Where: `ledger/billing.py:365-390`. An unknown customer returns silently, and a plan missing from\n  settings changes nothing.\n- Whose: on JusPrin 2's own site, ours. An event type we do not handle is ordinary and stays ignored.\n  Never made to happen.\n- Change: raise where the customer or the plan is not found.\n- **Simple.**\n\n**Guesses in billing.** Three if/else changes. The not-found case and the deletion stop were run only\nwith Chargebee patched.\n- Where:\n  - `ledger/billing.py:152-157`: any Chargebee failure reads as \"no card on file\";\n  - `:164-173`: on account deletion, \"subscription not found\" is taken as nothing to end;\n  - `ledger/reports.py:31-32`: any database conflict becomes \"This print already has a report.\"\n- Whose: Chargebee's \"not found\" is normal for an account with no customer on JusPrin 2's site.\n  Any other failure is ours. A deletion that cannot find the subscription comes to us, by the\n  directions. A conflict that is not the print's own report is ours.\n- Change:\n  - not-found means no card, anything else raises;\n  - deletion raises with the account and subscription in the error text;\n  - re-check `is_reported` and raise for any other conflict.\n- **Simple.**\n\n**The browser session is gone at checkout, or on the way back from paying.**\n- Where: `v2/web.py:297-302` and `:315-320`. A silent redirect to Credits and plans, even after paying.\n- Whose: the person's. Made to happen with Django's test client.\n- Change: render the existing page \"This link has expired. Go back to JusPrin and open the page\n  again.\" (`sign_in_result.html`, as in `v2/views.py:203-208`) with a log line.\n- **Simple**, if that page's heading is acceptable here. Words about the payment would need a new\n  sentence.\n\n**A wrong-scope or wrong-client token is told \"Sign in to JusPrin to continue.\"**\n- Where: `v2/auth.py:18-22`.\n- Whose: a token issued to another client, or without the scope, is ours, since our code is on both\n  ends. A deactivated account and an expired token stay the person's. Never made to happen.\n- Change: raise for the client mismatch, and for a token that verifies without the scope but not with\n  it.\n- **Simple.**\n\n**A lost link entry is told \"This link has expired\".**\n- Where: `v2/views.py:203-208`.\n- Whose: an entry the cache lost is ours. A link opened late or twice is the person's. Never made to\n  happen.\n- **Needs more.** The two cannot be told apart without a record of the links made.\n\n**JusPrin 1: a cancelled checkout raises a 500.**\n- Where: `jusprin_cb_views.py:59-60`.\n- Whose: the person's, if cancelling can reach this callback. Never made to happen.\n- Change: an if that sends a hosted page that did not succeed back to the pricing page.\n- **Simple.**\n\n**JusPrin 1 webhook: no plan and no account answers 200 with nothing logged.**\n- Where: `jusprin_cb_views.py:104-113`.\n- Whose: shown with crafted events. An ordinary first purchase can reach this path: Chargebee's event\n  comes before the browser's return, and the Chargebee address differs from the account's. A deleted\n  account's renewal reaches it too, and commit 2168e238ce chose to acknowledge that case. The lookup\n  by email also matches across products.\n- **Needs more.** Raising would report the ordinary first purchase. Keeping it quiet then, but not\n  later, needs a rule on the event's age that nobody has agreed. Limiting the email lookup to Obico\n  accounts would be a simple filter on its own.\n\n**JusPrin 1 checkout: a bare catch drops the Obico Pro discount.**\n- Where: `jusprin_cb_views.py:168-175`.\n- Whose: Chargebee not finding the subscription means no discount. Anything else is ours. Never made to\n  happen.\n- Change: catch only not-found, and let anything else raise.\n- **Simple.**\n\n**JusPrin 1 plan read: any failure answers a 500 with \"Failed to retrieve subscription plan\".**\n- Where: `views.py:46-70`.\n- Whose: ours. Never made to happen.\n- Change: delete the try/except.\n- **Simple.**\n\n**A provider refuses the person's own content.**\n- Where: `v2/gateway.py:323-330` (`UpstreamRefused`) and `:351-354`.\n- Whose: the person's. Inferred; which providers answer this way was never confirmed.\n- **Needs more.** It needs a new code from the server, handling in the app, and a sentence. That is\n  the server and the app together.\n\n**A renewal's card is declined.**\n- Where: `ledger/billing.py:290-294` grants nothing while an invoice is due, so the person sees \"This\n  message needs 1 credit; you have 0.\" while the page says the plan is renewing.\n- Whose: the person's. Never made to happen without Chargebee's Time Machine, which is shared.\n- **Needs more.** It needs a sentence, which is \"not yet\" in the directions.\n\n**A report photo in HEIC, or the server failing to read the upload.**\n- Where: `v2/views.py:233-241` (`_decodable`). Both answer \"That photo could not be read.\"\n- Whose: a picture Pillow cannot read is the person's. The server failing to read the uploaded file\n  is ours. A cut-off photo was made to happen; HEIC and a read failure were not.\n- Change: an if in the except, so an OS error carrying an error number raises.\n- **Simple.**\n\n**The AI provider fails after the message was charged.**\n- Where: `v2/credits.py:55`, `ledger/ledger.py:123`, `v2/gateway.py:191-195`. The charge stands.\n- Whose: ours. Shown with a replay test and a stalling provider stand-in.\n- **Needs more.** It changes what is charged.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"5da41084-c598-4f23-adde-ebea496dcc29","timestamp":"2026-11-25T18:39:50.465Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"## The server\n\n**The app sends something the server refuses** (a field a newer app added, a model removed from the\naliases, an empty alias setting).\n- Where: `v2/errors.py:68-76` (`REFUSALS`), `v2/gateway.py:206-211`, `v2/upstream.py`, and\n  `v2/views.py:172-175, 267-270`. Answered \"The request is not valid.\" or \"This model is not\n  available.\", with one log line of the code only.\n- Whose: ours, since our code is on both ends. Kenneth on 2026-11-15: \"Treat them as unexpected\n  errors.\" Never made to happen.\n- Change: raise in place of each refusal, so the top handler reports it. The app already treats the\n  server's error answer as ours.\n- **Simple.**\n\n**A paid Chargebee event that matches nothing.**\n- Where: `ledger/billing.py:365-390`. An unknown customer returns silently, and a plan missing from\n  settings changes nothing.\n- Whose: on JusPrin 2's own site, ours. An event type we do not handle is ordinary and stays ignored.\n  Never made to happen.\n- Change: raise where the customer or the plan is not found.\n- **Simple.**\n\n**Guesses in billing.** Three if/else changes. The not-found case and the deletion stop were run only\nwith Chargebee patched.\n- Where:\n  - `ledger/billing.py:152-157`: any Chargebee failure reads as \"no card on file\";\n  - `:164-173`: on account deletion, \"subscription not found\" is taken as nothing to end;\n  - `le