{"parentUuid":"e20aca7f-8bf3-4e20-82f9-f6197774991c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChQF2vRkVDeq3YDHdU8GD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014ECXuSkNXAGU2ukwcWhALU","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Fetch AI services' error docs","subagent_type":"web-fetch","prompt":"I need the documented HTTP error answers of three AI APIs, to decide in code which error answers are about the caller's own account, key, permissions, settings or limits, as opposed to a malformed request. Read these pages (follow to the current page if moved):\n- OpenRouter: https://openrouter.ai/docs/api-reference/errors (or https://openrouter.ai/docs/api/reference/errors-and-debugging) — list every HTTP status it documents, the shape of the error body (fields: code, message, metadata, any `error_type` field and ALL its documented values), and anything about 404 \"No endpoints found\" (data policy / privacy settings / BYOK) and 403 moderation.\n- Anthropic: https://docs.anthropic.com/en/api/errors (or https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/api/errors) — every status and its `type` value.\n- OpenAI: https://platform.openai.com/docs/guides/error-codes (API errors section) — every status, the error `code` / `type` values it names (e.g. invalid_api_key, insufficient_quota, unsupported_country_region_territory, model_not_found, rate_limit_exceeded), and for each what the docs say the cause is (key, account/org/project access, country, quota, request shape).\nReport as a compact table per service: status | type/code/error_type value | documented cause | quoted short phrase from docs. Say explicitly when a page could not be read and when a value is NOT documented. Do not guess values.","run_in_background":"true"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2960,"cache_read_input_tokens":210697,"output