{"parentUuid":"c570bcee-4594-41db-99da-8b6a6f149e83","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"a87f93ac-7f7c-43ec-a4cd-0785d69b9cce","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TVTF3HnGH2yKueTYsenUAT","type":"tool_result","content":"161:### Nine need one line of text that shows another side's own words\n162-\n163-Kenneth approved the form on 2026-11-24: the name, then its words in quotation marks, as in\n164-`OpenRouter says: “…”` (\"Name, then its words\"). The string does not exist in the code today. Adding\n165-it is one translatable string plus its translations. Each place then still needs its own decision\n166-that the refusal is the person's.\n167-\n168-- Autosave: disk full or a folder that cannot be written shows \"Changes couldn't be saved. JusPrin\n169-  will retry.\" with the system's reason dropped. `Workspace/ProjectAutosave.cpp:351`,\n170-  `Shell/StatusRow.cpp:616`. Also repeats every 2 seconds (see the repeating group).\n171-- Export, restore, version history: \"The project couldn't be exported. Try again.\" and two like it.\n172-  `Shell/LeftPaneProject.cpp:161-168` and its two neighbours.\n173-- Opening a project: one sentence covers a project another JusPrin window holds, a save the system\n174-  refused, and a damaged project. `Workspace/ProjectAutosave.cpp:952-954`. The damaged project\n175-  alone is a simple rethrow. The other-window case needs a sentence (asked, see below).\n176-- The projects folder cannot be read: `Home/OrcaHomeBackend.cpp:1019`. Also repeats every second.\n177-- Save on a proposal card: `AgentUI/src/components/ProposalCard.tsx:31-32`. Also needs the press\n178-  handled as the person's click and not as a tool call by the model.\n179-- The service behind the person's own key names a cause (country, moderation, spending limit, no\n180-  access to the model): shown today as \"Something went wrong on our side\" and reported.\n181-  `Agent/ProviderAgent.cpp:874-890`.\n182-- Exporting kept G-code from Print history to a full, locked or unplugged card:\n183-  `Shell/GcodeHistoryRecorder.cpp:454`, reached from `Home/OrcaHomeBackend.cpp:1337, 1360, 1496`.\n184-- An attachment that cannot be read: `Agent/AgentHost.cpp:1622-1637`.\n185-- The person's own service answers HTTP 429: its words, which may name a daily cap, are dropped.\n186-  `Agent/ProviderAgent.cpp:888-889, 783`.\n187-\n188-### Nine need a new sentence of ours\n189-\n190-A sentence we write for the person needs Kenneth's yes, quoted in the commit message. None of these\n191-nine has been seen in the running app, so each must be made to happen before he is asked.\n192-\n193-- Email sign-in: an address not yet confirmed, and a deactivated account, both show \"JusPrin\n194-  couldn't sign you in. Try again.\" `Agent/CloudAccount.cpp:313-314`.\n195-- Home will not start on a Windows computer without WebView2: `Home/HomeWebView.cpp:85`. (Lines\n196-  `:80` and `:177` of the same file are ours and are simple reports.)\n197-- A chat that is too long: \"The request was too large for the OpenAI service.\" names no next step.\n198-  `Agent/ProviderAgent.cpp:789`. Asked, see below.\n199-- A Klipper printer whose Moonraker needs an API key shows \"… isn't answering.\"\n200-  `Home/OrcaHomeBackend.cpp:318`. Reproduce with the Docker Moonraker in `tests/printer_hosts/`.\n201-- The printer window shows \"Nothing answered at …\" for every page error.\n202-  `Home/PrinterWindow.cpp:167-182`.\n203-- A file dropped on Home or on the chat that the page cannot read (Windows and Linux).\n204-  `HomeUI/src/App.tsx:218`, `AgentUI/src/App.tsx:311-314`. Also needs a message from the page.\n205-- An unreadable OrcaSlicer settings file is read as \"no printers\". `Home/OrcaImport.cpp:67`.\n206-- A plan whose renewal payment was declined: the chat says \"This message needs 1 credit; you have\n207-  0.\" and the page says the plan renews. Server `ledger/billing.py:290-294`. Do not use Chargebee's\n208-  Time Machine to reproduce it; the test site is shared.\n209-- An AI provider refuses the person's own content: server `v2/gateway.py:323-330, 351-354`. Needs\n210-  the server and the app together.\n211-\n212-### Four repeat, so reporting them needs a memory of what was already reported\n213-\n214-- The update check: `Updates/UpdateCheck.cpp:102-115, 126-136`. A rate limit from GitHub is not\n215-  ours and shares \"Couldn't reach GitHub\". GitHub's error text names the person's IP address, which\n216-  must not go into a report.\n217-- The AI panel will not start: `Agent/AgentWebView.cpp:237-241, 322-332, 385`. The handshake timer\n218-  fires again after 20 seconds and on every Retry. A missing WebView2 is the person's.\n219-- The history cleanup after each save: `Workspace/ProjectAutosave.cpp:455`.\n220-- A kept G-code file that changed on disk: `Home/OrcaHomeBackend.cpp:1246`.\n221-\n222-Autosave and the projects folder (above) repeat too.\n223-\n224-A proposal, read in the code and not run, not approved: `report_unexpected` in\n225-`Support/ErrorReport.cpp` already drops a failure it has asked about in this run (same `doing` and\n226-`error`, lines 112-114), but only on the path that shows the dialog. With automatic reports on, it\n227-sends every repeat. Making that one check apply to both paths might cover all six repeating places\n228-with no record at any of them.\n229-\n230-### Two tell the page only \"worked or not\"\n231-\n232-The page cannot say whose failure it was without a new field in the answer it gets.\n233-\n234-- Credits and plans, and Billing and usage, will not open: `Shell/ServerSheet.cpp:86-96`.\n235-- Delete account: `Agent/ModelCatalogFetch.cpp:143-163`, shown by\n236-  `AgentUI/src/components/Preferences.tsx:310`.\n237-\n238-### Two need a change in OrcaSlicer's own code\n239-\n240-Read `agent-docs/jusprin/fork-stewardship.md` before touching either.\n241-","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"c01c99c0-113d-4a2b-af2f-7c885ddb9e5d","timestamp":"2026-11-25T20:08:53.704Z","toolUseResult