{"parentUuid":"c26df268-3c09-40e8-adda-5fd7f1338b25","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChQGKyCmrKUPAhq5o3kCX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"While the build waits, I'm writing the parts of the notes file that don't depend on the \"after\" runs."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":502,"cache_read_input_tokens":331568,"output_tokens":1165,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":67},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":502,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1165,"cache_read_input_tokens":331568,"cache_creation_input_tokens":502,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":502},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"bd9ae7b2-a267-4c23-b308-36be1f69317c","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011ChQGKxzdCCq97WGwXL18W","requestRef":"986d0052-2f42-425d-8c6b-7462feb0fe41","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"1db5373c-440b-472f-ad86-76e11075f633","timestamp":"2026-11-25T20:19:05.643Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","madeBy":"model","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/misrouted-failures","sessionId":"b575a9e5-080c-46d7-b71a-f5842e099a04","version":"2.1.330","gitBranch":"claude/misrouted-failures","slug":"linear-finding-kay-of-b575a9e5-080c-46d7-b71a-f5842e099a04","dataFlowOn":true}
{"parentUuid":"1db5373c-440b-472f-ad86-76e11075f633","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChQGKyCmrKUPAhq5o3kCX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NRD6URaw44MtZwmWNrXkBX","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/kenneth/Library/Application Support/Claude/side-session-notes/local_cd3120f7-030a-4af8-a6d1-28ecae789f1a/misrouted-failures-says-changes.md","content":"# The \"X says: “…”\" line, and the places that need only it (2026-11-25)\n\nKenneth asked for the places that need only the line that shows another side's own words (\"tell the\nmain session to do these simple cases, withe your propoesd wording\"). The wording is the one he\napproved on 2026-11-24, \"Name, then its words\": `%1% says: “%2%”`.\n\nAFTER_COUNTS\n\n**Where the work is.** The worktree `/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/misrouted-failures`,\non top of `e5244801be`, uncommitted. The full diff is `misrouted-failures-says-changes-app.patch` in this\nfolder.\n\n**How each failure was made to happen.**\n- The scratch copy of the built app at `e5244801be` (`says-before.app`) ran with its own data folder.\n- A stand-in program on 127.0.0.1:18731 answered in place of the AI service, replaying the answer for\n  each case. It also collected every Sentry report the app sent.\n- For the G-code export, a 60 MB disk image (`JPCARD`) was attached read-only.\n- Nothing went to a real Sentry project or to a real AI service.\n- Evidence: `/private/tmp/claude/claude-502/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/b575a9e5-080c-46d7-b71a-f5842e099a04/scratchpad/live/runs/<case>-before` and `-after`\n  (the page's messages, the stand-in's answers, the reports received, the app's log).\n\n## The line itself\n\nA new header, `Support/SaidBy.hpp`, holds the one function, `said_by(name, words)`. It only\nformats. It also holds a constant, `kSystemName` (\"macOS\", \"Windows\" or \"Linux\"), for the places\nwhere the operating system is the one speaking. The function is:\n\n```cpp\ninline std::string said_by(const std::string& name, const std::string& words)\n{\n    // TRN %1% is an AI provider or the operating system, such as OpenAI or macOS. %2% is what it answered, in its own words and language.\n    return Slic3r::format(translated(L(\"%1% says: “%2%”\")), name, words);\n}\n```\n\n`update_catalogs.py` added the entry to `JusPrin.pot` and to the 22 native catalogs. The 22\ntranslations are the ones from the reverted work, each marked `# AI Translated`, and every catalog\npasses `msgfmt --check-format --check-header`. The same run also moved one entry to the obsolete\nentries in every catalog: \"The printer profiles could not be read: %1%\". That string left the code in\n`e5244801be`, but the catalogs were not updated then.\n\nOnly the message text the service sent goes into `%2%`, never the whole answer, and it stays in the\nservice's language.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":502,"cache_read_input_tokens":331568,"output_tokens":1165,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":67},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":502,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1165,"cache_read_input_tokens":331568,"cache_creation_input_tokens":502,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":502},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":9730,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01NRD6URaw44MtZwmWNrXkBX":{"file_path":"/Users/kenneth/Library/Application Support/Claude/side-session-notes/local_cd3120f7-030a-4af8-a6d1-28ecae789f1a/misrouted-failures-says-changes.md","content":"# The \"X says: “…”\" line, and the places that need only it (2026-11-25)\n\nKenneth asked for the places that need only the line that shows another side's own words (\"tell the\nmain session to do these simple cases, withe your propoesd wording\"). The wording is the one he\napproved on 2026-11-24, \"Name, then its words\": `%1% says: “%2%”`.\n\nAFTER_COUNTS\n\n**Where the work is.** The worktree `/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/misrouted-failures`,\non top of `e5244801be`, uncommitted. The full diff is `misrouted-failures-says-changes-app.patch` in this\nfolder.\n\n**How each failure was made to happen.**\n- The scratch copy of the built app at `e5244801be` (`says-before.app`) ran with its own data folder.\n- A stand-in program on 127.0.0.1:18731 answered in place of the AI service, replaying the answer for\n  each case. It also collected every Sentry report the app sent.\n- For the G-code export, a 60 MB disk image (`JPCARD`) was attached read-only.\n- Nothing went to a real Sentry project or to a real AI service.\n- Evidence: `/private/tmp/claude/claude-502/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/b575a9e5-080c-46d7-b71a-f5842e099a04/scratchpad/live/runs/<case>-before` and `-after`\n  (the page's messages, the stand-in's answers, the reports received, the app's log).\n\n## The line itself\n\nA new header, `Support/SaidBy.hpp`, holds the one function, `said_by(name, words)`. It only\nformats. It also holds a constant, `kSystemName` (\"macOS\", \"Windows\" or \"Linux\"), for the places\nwhere the operating system is the one speaking. The function is:\n\n```cpp\ninline std::string said_by(const std::string& name, const std::string& words)\n{\n    // TRN %1% is an AI provider or the operating system, such as OpenAI or macOS. %2% is what it answered, in its own words and language.\n    return Slic3r::format(translated(L(\"%1% says: “%2%”\")), name, words);\n}\n```\n\n`update_catalogs.py` added the entry to `JusPrin.pot` and to the 22 native catalogs. The 22\ntranslations are the ones from the reverted work, each marked `# AI Translated`, and every catalog\npasses `msgfmt --check-format --check-header`. The same run also moved one entry to the obsolete\nentries in every catalog: \"The printer profiles could not be read: %1%\". That string left the code in\n`e5244801be`, but the catalogs were not updated then.\n\nOnly the message text the service sent goes into `%2%`, never the whole answer, and it stays in the\nservice's language.\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"bd9ae7b2-a267-4c23-b308-36be1f69317c","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011ChQGKxzdCCq97WGwXL18W","requestRef":"986d0052-2f42-425d-8c6b-7462feb0fe41","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"8e3a8f59-760d-439d-9ca3-1c5025d466b2","timestamp":"2026-11-25T20:19:15.374Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","madeBy":"model","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/misrouted-failures","sessionId":"b575a9e5-080c-46d7-b71a-f5842e099a04","version":"2.1.330","gitBranch":"claude/misrouted-failures","slug":"linear-finding-kay-of-b575a9e5-080c-46d7-b71a-f5842e099a04","dataFlowOn":true}
{"type":"file-history-delta","messageId":"8e3a8f59-760d-439d-9ca3-1c5025d466b2","snapshotMessageId":"8d5554c4-8c53-4eac-b27a-8513dc276acd","trackingPath":"/Users/kenneth/Library/Application Support/Claude/side-session-notes/local_cd3120f7-030a-4af8-a6d1-28ecae789f1a/misrouted-failures-says-changes.md","backup":{"backupFileName":null,"version":1,"backupTime":"2026-11-25T20:19:15.393Z","realParentDir":"/Users/kenneth/Library/Application Support/Claude/side-session-notes/local_cd3120f7-030a-4af8-a6d1-28ecae789f1a"},"timestamp":"2026-11-25T20:19:15.393Z"}
{"parentUuid":"8e3a8f59-760d-439d-9ca3-1c5025d466b2","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"a87f93ac-7f7c-43ec-a4cd-0785d69b9cce","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NRD6URaw44MtZwmWNrXkBX","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /Users/kenneth/Library/Application Support/Claude/side-session-notes/local_cd3120f7-030a-4af8-a6d1-28ecae789f1a/misrouted-failures-says-changes.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"beaca764-a9b9-49de-a9a3-aa0e04e61bee","timestamp":"2026-11-25T20:19:15.406Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/Users/kenneth/Library/Application Support/Claude/side-session-notes/local_cd3120f7-030a-4af8-a6d1-28ecae789f1a/misrouted-failures-says-changes.md","content":"# The \"X says: “…”\" line, and the places that need only it (2026-11-25)\n\nKenneth asked for the places that need only the line that shows another side's own words (\"tell the\nmain session to do these simple cases, withe your propoesd wording\"). The wording is the one he\napproved on 2026-11-24, \"Name, then its words\": `%1% says: “%2%”`.\n\nAFTER_COUNTS\n\n**Where the work is.** The worktree `/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/misrouted-failures`,\non top of `e5244801be`, uncommitted. The full diff is `misrouted-failures-says-changes-app.patch` in this\nfolder.\n\n**How each failure was made to happen.**\n- The scratch copy of the built app at `e5244801be` (`says-before.app`) ran with its own data folder.\n- A stand-in program on 127.0.0.1:18731 answered in place of the AI service, replaying the answer for\n  each case. It also collected every Sentry report the app sent.\n- For the G-code export, a 60 MB disk image (`JPCARD`) was attached read-only.\n- Nothing went to a real Sentry project or to a real AI service.\n- Evidence: `/private/tmp/claude/claude-502/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/b575a9e5-080c-46d7-b71a-f5842e099a04/scratchpad/live/runs/<case>-before` and `-after`\n  (the page's messages, the stand-in's answers, the reports received, the app's log).\n\n## The line itself\n\nA new header, `Support/SaidBy.hpp`, holds the one function, `said_by(name, words)`. It only\nformats. It also holds a constant, `kSystemName` (\"macOS\", \"Windows\" or \"Linux\"), for the places\nwhere the operating system is the one speaking. The function is:\n\n```cpp\ninline std::string said_by(const std::string& name, const std::string& words)\n{\n    // TRN %1% is an AI provider or the operating system, such as OpenAI or macOS. %2% is what it answered, in its own words and language.\n    return Slic3r::format(translated(L(\"%1% says: “%2%”\")), name, words);\n}\n```\n\n`update_catalogs.py` added the entry to `JusPrin.pot` and to the 22 native catalogs. The 22\ntranslations are the ones from the reverted work, each marked `# AI Translated`, and every catalog\npasses `msgfmt --check-format --check-header`. The same run also moved one entry to the obsolete\nentries in every catalog: \"The printer profiles could not be read: %1%\". That string left the code in\n`e5244801be`, but the catalogs were not updated then.\n\nOnly the message text the service sent goes into `%2%`, never the whole answer, and it stays in the\nservice's language.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8e3a8f59-760d-439d-9ca3-1c5025d466b2","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/misrouted-failures","sessionId":"b575a9e5-080c-46d7-b71a-f5842e099a04","version":"2.1.330","gitBranch":"claude/misrouted-failures","slug":"linear-finding-kay-of-b575a9e5-080c-46d7-b71a-f5842e099a04","dataFlowOn":true}
